# Network games where the host and the client use different fonts (Traditional on the host,
# Futuristic on the client): the host lays a screen out with its own font, so every text item's
# box is exactly as wide as the text in the host's font (Text::draw_wrapped adds one item per line
# and per linked phrase, such as the club name next to the player's name). In the client's wider
# font the text no longer fits, and the text box draw (0x5e6d80) cuts a line that does not fit
# back to its last space: a one-word club name is cut to nothing, longer texts lose words.
# On a network client only, a box that does not wrap now keeps its whole text (it can run a few
# pixels past the box). Host, single player and wrapping boxes do as before. Code in .nick at 0xdf2040.
